  "statement": "[RF-REACTIVE-CONTEXT-ASSEMBLY-R2] No Pi consumer shall fabricate structure over rf context read envelopes: a component's block is read from attributed block records, never sentinel text regexed out of a full context-show envelope (adopt context show --block KEY when rfc-s24ro.3 ships; open, unshipped), and absent context diff keys are reported missing, never synthesized or rendered as constant fallbacks (adopt context diff --detail compact when rfc-s24ro.4 ships; open, unshipped) - pin docs/programs/reactive-context-assembly-2026-10-18/02-swarm-usage-and-command-grammar.md:38@6a251bf73af5",
  "quote": "The consumer used text sentinel extraction rather than block attribution; this was its own workaround, with prospective spoof/format risk. Proposed computation: a **materialized component output query** `(render ID, component ID, occurrence key, audience)` whose return includes only the authorized attributed blocks and digest, not a speculative free-text grep.",
  "citation": "docs/programs/reactive-context-assembly-2026-10-18/02-swarm-usage-and-command-grammar.md:38@6a251bf73af5",
